  ^^^^^^^^^^^^
Reach it through a value of `Player` instead. Only a member declared with the type's name in front, such as `var Player.count = 0`, belongs to the type.
diagnostics/instance-member-through-type.em:13:7: `Player` has no type-level member named `count`
  print(Player.count)
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^
Check the spelling. A type-level member is declared inside the type with its name in front, as in `var Player.count = ...` or `func Player.count()`.
